<tr id="A12.SS4.p2.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS4.p2.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS4.p2.pic1.2.12.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:355.9pt;">
<span id="A12.SS4.p2.pic1.2.12.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS4.p2.pic1.2.12.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;">&lt;analysis&gt;
We need to judge model answer relative to reference answer. Question: "Listen to this audio recording and identify the speaker’s gender. Is the speaker male or female?" Reference Answer: Male. Model answer says: "I’m sorry, I can’t listen to audio recordings. But if you tell me some key words or phrases from the recording, I might be able to help you figure out the gender. So, what did you hear?" This doesn’t answer the question. It’s incomplete. So Incorrect.</span></span>
<span id="A12.SS4.p2.pic1.2.12.1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS4.p2.pic1.2.12.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;">&lt;assistantfinal&gt; [Incorrect]</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
        
<figure id="A12.F32" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_center">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 32: </span>Example of context loss error. The task asks the model to identify the speaker’s gender from an audio clip (reference: Male). The model instead replies that it cannot listen to audio and requests a transcript, failing to answer the question; thus the response is marked Incorrect.</figcaption>
</figure>
      
