<span id="A12.SS4.p4.pic1.2.11.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS4.p4.pic1.2.11.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Model Judegement:</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS4.p4.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS4.p4.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS4.p4.pic1.2.12.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:355.9pt;">
<span id="A12.SS4.p4.pic1.2.12.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS4.p4.pic1.2.12.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;">&lt;analysis&gt;
We need to compare the model answer to the reference answer. The question: "Listen to this audio clip and choose the first word that relates to a currency name. Is it A. between, B. us, C. us dollar, or D. pounds?" … Model answer says: "So the answer is C. US dollar." That doesn’t match. Model answer says C, but the question’s answer is "US" (probably B). So it’s incorrect. Also the explanation incorrectly describes exchange rates. So answer is Incorrect.</span></span>
<span id="A12.SS4.p4.pic1.2.12.1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS4.p4.pic1.2.12.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;">&lt;assistantfinal&gt; [Incorrect]</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
