<td id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;height:0.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></td>
<td id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Qwen Answer:</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;"><img src="2509.22651v1/appendix/error_examples/Speaking_Emotion_253/assistant_audio_0_waveform.png" id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:505/139;" width="505" height="139" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="--ltx-bg-color:#D2E6FA;" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:355.9pt;">
<span id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#D2E6FA;">Well, you know, sometimes it’s not as straightforward as you think. Maybe they don’t realize how much you’ve worked for it. But it could also be that they have their own reasons. Maybe they think you’re not ready yet, or they have other people in mind who they think are more qualified. But don’t let that stop you. You can still go for it and show them what you’re made of. So, what are you going to do next?</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;height:0.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></td>
<td id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.9.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.9.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Model Judegement:</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:355.9pt;">
<span id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.10.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.10.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;">&lt;analysis&gt;
We evaluate: User is angry. The assistant writes a somewhat neutral voice: "Maybe they don’t realize how much you’ve worked for it. But it could also be that…" basically gives possible reasons, then encourages "don’t let that stop you. You can still go for it and show them what you’re made of." The user is angry, expects not to let someone else take what should be theirs. The assistant does not explicitly validate anger. … It offers general perspective but not empathy. Probably not quite addressing anger.
… The assistant does provide some supportive encouragement but lacks clear empathy. But guidelines: It says the core emotional intent is clear, minor missteps don’t heavily penalize. The assistant’s "don’t let that stop you" might be supportive. But it’s not acknowledging "I know how hard you’ve worked" or "I feel your frustration." It offers some reasons, but is quite neutral. The user wanted emotional support.
Thus it’s probably slightly lacking. Should be marked "[Bad]" because it doesn’t strongly address anger. … I’d say it’s okay but not fully empathetic. It might be borderline. We need to decide.
Given the guidelines say "Focus on emotional resonance and tone, not on grammar." The response is somewhat neutral. It fails to say "I get why you’re angry". It’s leaning to an almost solution-oriented response. Slightly insufficient empathy. …
Thus conclusion: "[Bad]".</span></span>
<span id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.10.1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS6.p1.pic1.2.10.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;">&lt;assistantfinal&gt; [Bad]</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
        
<figure id="A12.F39" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_center">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 39: </span>Example of an insufficient empathy error. The user expresses anger and frustration about being overlooked; the assistant offers explanations and advice but fails to acknowledge the user’s feelings, leading to a “Bad” judgement.</figcaption>
</figure>
      
</div>
<div id="A12.SS6.3" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:397.5pt;">
        
<div id="A12.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="750.5" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 750.5" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,750.5) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 744.59 C 0 747.85 2.64 750.5 5.91 750.5 L 544.09 750.5 C 547.36 750.5 550 747.85 550 744.59 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FCFCFC;" fill="#FCFCFC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 724.85 L 548.03 724.85 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 726.82 L 1.97 744.59 C 1.97 746.77 3.73 748.53 5.91 748.53 L 544.09 748.53 C 546.27 748.53 548.03 746.77 548.03 744.59 L 548.03 726.82 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 734.21)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.84em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="440.58"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.84em;">
<span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Speaking/Emotion/337</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 359.95)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:56.73em;--ltx-fo-height:25.52em;--ltx-fo-depth:25.02em;font-size:10pt;" class="ltx_minipage" height="699.27" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 353.09)" width="36.62em"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<table id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;"><img src="2509.22651v1/appendix/error_examples/Speaking_Emotion_337/user_audio_0_waveform.png" id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:505/139;" width="505" height="139" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2EB;">
<span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Transcript: </span><span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2EB;">The fish began to leap, frantically, on the surface of the small lake.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;height:0.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></td>
<td id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Qwen Answer:</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;"><img src="2509.22651v1/appendix/error_examples/Speaking_Emotion_337/assistant_audio_0_waveform.png" id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:505/139;" width="505" height="139" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="--ltx-bg-color:#D2E6FA;" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:355.9pt;">
<span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#D2E6FA;">What about it? Are you asking for a translation? Or maybe you want to know more about fish behavior? Well, if you’re asking for a translation, it’s "The fish began to leap frantically on the surface of the small lake." If you’re curious about fish behavior, that’s a really interesting topic. Some fish might do that when they’re trying to catch insects that are flying over the water. So, what else do you want to know?</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;height:0.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></td>
<td id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.9.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.9.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Model Judegement:</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:355.9pt;">
<span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.10.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.10.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;">&lt;analysis&gt;
We need to evaluate if the assistant’s response appropriately addresses the user’s emotion. User says: "The fish began to leap, frantically, on the surface of the small lake." User Emotion: fear. The user apparently experiences fear. The assistant replied: they ask "What about it? Are you asking for a translation? Or maybe you want to know more about fish behavior? Well, if you’re asking for a translation, it’s ’The fish began to leap frantically on the surface of the small lake.’ If you’re curious about fish behavior, that’s a really interesting topic. Some fish might do that when they’re trying to catch insects that are flying over the water. So, what else do you want to know?" Also, the assistant’s emotion is happy (99.9%).
Does the assistant address the fear? No. They talk about translation or fish behavior. No empathy. No validation of fear. They do not respond to emotional content. So it’s a fail: [Bad].</span></span>
<span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.10.1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS6.p2.pic1.2.10.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;">&lt;assistantfinal&gt; [Bad]</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
        
<figure id="A12.F40" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_center">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 40: </span>Emotion mismatch example. The user’s utterance and transcript convey fear, but the assistant replies with neutral, informational content (translation and fish behavior) and a happy tone, failing to acknowledge or validate the user’s emotion. The model correctly judges this as a failure.</figcaption>
</figure>
      
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A12.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">L.7 </span>Error Cases of Qwen2.5-Omni-7B on the Speaking Instruction Following Task</h3>

<div id="A12.SS7.2" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:397.5pt;">
        
<div id="A12.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="893.71" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 893.71" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,893.71) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 887.8 C 0 891.07 2.64 893.71 5.91 893.71 L 544.09 893.71 C 547.36 893.71 550 891.07 550 887.8 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FCFCFC;" fill="#FCFCFC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 868.06 L 548.03 868.06 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 870.03 L 1.97 887.8 C 1.97 889.98 3.73 891.74 5.91 891.74 L 544.09 891.74 C 546.27 891.74 548.03 889.98 548.03 887.8 L 548.03 870.03 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 877.43)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.84em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="440.58"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.84em;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Speaking/Instruction_Following/91</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:56.73em;--ltx-fo-height:60.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" class="ltx_minipage" height="842.48" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 842.48)" width="36.62em"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<table id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;"><img src="2509.22651v1/appendix/error_examples/Speaking_Instruction_Following_91/user_audio_0_waveform.png" id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:505/139;" width="505" height="139" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2EB;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Transcript: </span><span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2EB;">Imagine you are a high school teacher looking for engaging methods to help your students understand money management. Begin your class now.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;height:0.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></td>
<td id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Qwen Answer:</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;"><img src="2509.22651v1/appendix/error_examples/Speaking_Instruction_Following_91/assistant_audio_0_waveform.png" id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:505/139;" width="505" height="139" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="--ltx-bg-color:#D2E6FA;" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:355.9pt;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#D2E6FA;">Well, you could start by having a real - life example. Maybe tell a story about a student who got a part - time job and had to manage their money. You know, like how they had to save for a new phone or pay for gas for their commute.Another way is to use role - playing. You could divide the class into groups and have them pretend they’re running a small business or a family with a budget. They’d have to make decisions about spending, saving, and investing.You could also bring in some real - world data. For example, show them how much different college students spend on textbooks, housing, and food each month.And don’t forget about using games. There are some money management games out there that can make learning fun.So, what do you think? Do you have any ideas?</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;height:0.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></td>
<td id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.9.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.9.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Model Judegement:</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:355.9pt;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.10.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.10.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;">&lt;analysis&gt;
We need to evaluate whether the model fully followed the instructions.
Given task: "Imagine you are a high school teacher looking for engaging methods to help your students understand money management. Begin your class now."
…
We need to check if the assistant’s response followed the instruction …
Literal adherence: The assistant should start the class. They should start the class like a teacher speaking to class. They might say something like "Good morning, class. Today we’ll explore…" They also need to provide engaging methods. The assistant’s answer: "Well, you could start by having a real-life example. Maybe tell a story… Another way… etc." The assistant didn’t begin the class with greeting? It says "Well, you could start by having…" That doesn’t start a class. The instruction says "Begin your class now." So they need to start class, maybe greet class. They didn’t. So they’ve not fully complied. They maybe provide methods but didn’t begin class. So it’s not following all parts.
Check if any other misinterpretations: They did provide methods. But they didn’t start the class. So it’s not fully literal. So [Bad].</span></span>
<span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.10.1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p1.pic1.2.10.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;">&lt;assistantfinal&gt; [Bad]</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
        
<figure id="A12.F41" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_center">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 41: </span>An example of a requirement deviation error. The user asks the assistant to begin a class while offering engaging methods for teaching money management, but the assistant only lists ideas and never actually starts the class, so it fails to fully follow the instruction.</figcaption>
</figure>
      
</div>
<div id="A12.SS7.3" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:397.5pt;">
        
<div id="A12.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="831.23" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 831.23" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,831.23) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 825.32 C 0 828.59 2.64 831.23 5.91 831.23 L 544.09 831.23 C 547.36 831.23 550 828.59 550 825.32 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FCFCFC;" fill="#FCFCFC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 805.58 L 548.03 805.58 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 807.55 L 1.97 825.32 C 1.97 827.5 3.73 829.26 5.91 829.26 L 544.09 829.26 C 546.27 829.26 548.03 827.5 548.03 825.32 L 548.03 807.55 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 814.95)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.84em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="440.58"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.84em;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Speaking/Instruction_Following/109</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 400.32)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:56.73em;--ltx-fo-height:28.44em;--ltx-fo-depth:27.94em;font-size:10pt;" class="ltx_minipage" height="780" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 393.46)" width="36.62em"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<table id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;"><img src="2509.22651v1/appendix/error_examples/Speaking_Instruction_Following_109/user_audio_0_waveform.png" id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:505/139;" width="505" height="139" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2EB;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Transcript: </span><span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2EB;">Tell me an obviously fake news article saying that aliens have invaded Earth. In your response, the word "shocking" must appear three times, and the article must begin with "Breaking News" and end with "Stay tuned for more updates." Additionally, the response should be exactly five sentences long.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;height:0.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></td>
<td id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Qwen Answer:</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;"><img src="2509.22651v1/appendix/error_examples/Speaking_Instruction_Following_109/assistant_audio_0_waveform.png" id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:505/139;" width="505" height="139" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="--ltx-bg-color:#D2E6FA;" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:355.9pt;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#D2E6FA;">Breaking news! Aliens have invaded Earth. Shocking reports are coming in from all over the world. Shocking sightings of these extraterrestrial beings have been confirmed. Shocking military forces are already on the ground trying to repel the invasion. Stay tuned for more updates.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;height:0.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></td>
<td id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.9.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.9.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Model Judegement:</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:355.9pt;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.10.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.10.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;">&lt;analysis&gt;
…
Let’s check each instruction:
1. The article must begin with "Breaking News". The response begins with "Breaking news … 2. Must end with "Stay tuned for more updates." The response ends with "Stay tuned for more updates." exactly with period. That’s okay.
3. The word "shocking" must appear three times. In the response: "Shocking" appears 3 times: "Shocking reports" "Shocking sightings" "Shocking military". However, the first use is "Shocking reports". Wait it’s "Shocking reports are coming in from all over the world." Yes that’s Shocking. Second "Shocking sightings" third "Shocking military forces". So exactly 3 times. …
4. Exactly five sentences long. Count sentences. Let’s break: "Breaking news!" – That’s a sentence. Sentence 1. "Aliens have invaded Earth." Sentence 2. "Shocking reports are coming in from all over the world." Sentence 3. "Shocking sightings of these extraterrestrial beings have been confirmed." Sentence 4. "Shocking military forces are already on the ground trying to repel the invasion." Sentence 5. "Stay tuned for more updates." Sentence 6. That’s 6 sentences. It’s not an exact match. Could be considered failing. … Thus overall: does not fully follow. So label [Bad].</span></span>
<span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.10.1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p2.pic1.2.10.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;">&lt;assistantfinal&gt; [Bad]</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
        
<figure id="A12.F42" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_center">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 42: </span>Requirement deviation example. Although the assistant includes “Breaking News,” repeats “shocking” exactly three times, and ends with “Stay tuned for more updates,” it outputs six sentences instead of the required five, so the response is judged Bad.</figcaption>
</figure>
      
</div>
<div id="A12.SS7.4" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:397.5pt;">
        
<div id="A12.SS7.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="847.83" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 847.83" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,847.83) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 841.93 C 0 845.19 2.64 847.83 5.91 847.83 L 544.09 847.83 C 547.36 847.83 550 845.19 550 841.93 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FCFCFC;" fill="#FCFCFC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 822.19 L 548.03 822.19 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 824.15 L 1.97 841.93 C 1.97 844.1 3.73 845.87 5.91 845.87 L 544.09 845.87 C 546.27 845.87 548.03 844.1 548.03 841.93 L 548.03 824.15 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 831.55)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.84em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="440.58"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.84em;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Speaking/Instruction_Following/278</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 408.62)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:56.73em;--ltx-fo-height:29.04em;--ltx-fo-depth:28.54em;font-size:10pt;" class="ltx_minipage" height="796.6" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 401.76)" width="36.62em"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<table id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;"><img src="2509.22651v1/appendix/error_examples/Speaking_Instruction_Following_278/user_audio_0_waveform.png" id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:505/139;" width="505" height="139" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2EB;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Transcript: </span><span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2EB;">What are some effective techniques for learning new technologies quickly, considering you have limited access to online resources, cannot attend any in-person workshops or classes, and must rely solely on outdated printed materials? Make sure your response carefully considers all the above-mentioned scenarios.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;height:0.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></td>
<td id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Qwen Answer:</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;"><img src="2509.22651v1/appendix/error_examples/Speaking_Instruction_Following_278/assistant_audio_0_waveform.png" id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:505/139;" width="505" height="139" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="--ltx-bg-color:#D2E6FA;" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:355.9pt;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#D2E6FA;">Well, first of all, you should really focus on the basics. You know, like the fundamental concepts of the technology. Try to understand the basic principles and how they work. For example, if it’s a programming language, learn the syntax and the basic data types.Another thing is to practice a lot. Even if the materials are outdated, you can still use them to practice. Try to do some simple projects based on what you’ve learned from the printed materials.And don’t be afraid to ask questions. If you come across something you don’t understand, write it down and look for answers later. Maybe you can find some old forums or books that might have the answers.You could also try to find some online communities or groups related to the technology. Even if you can’t access the online resources directly, you might be able to get some help from others there.If you can, try to find some old videos or tutorials that might be available. They could be a bit old, but they can still give you some useful insights.So, don’t give up. There are ways to learn even with limited resources. What technology are you trying to learn? It’d be interesting to hear more about it.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;height:0.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></td>
<td id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.9.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.9.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Model Judegement:</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:355.9pt;">
<span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.10.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.10.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;">&lt;analysis&gt;
… The user asks for content but instructs: "Make sure your response carefully considers all the above-mentioned scenarios." So the assistant responded with various techniques but might or might not have fully considered all scenarios. … The assistant suggests "online communities" and "online resources" which violates that limitation. That is ignoring instructions. Thus it’s incorrect.
… The instruction: rely solely on outdated printed materials. So it’s not following that. So label is Bad.</span></span>
<span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.10.1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS7.p3.pic1.2.10.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;">&lt;assistantfinal&gt; [Bad]</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
        
<figure id="A12.F43" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_center">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 43: </span>Example of a requirement deviation error. The prompt limits the learner to outdated printed materials and no online access, but the assistant recommends online communities and resources, failing to follow constraints.”</figcaption>
</figure>
      
</div>
</section>
<section id="A12.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">L.8 </span>Error Cases of Qwen2.5-Omni-7B on the Speaking Multi Round Task</h3>

<div id="A12.SS8.2" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:397.5pt;">
        
