</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2EB;">
<span id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Transcript: </span><span id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2EB;">Can you help me arrange these amounts of money in ascending order: 5 yuan, 4 yuan and 50 cents, 80 cents, 10 cents, and 2 yuan and 50 cents?</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;height:0.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></td>
<td id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Qwen Answer:</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;"><img src="2509.22651v1/appendix/error_examples/Speaking_Multi_Round_152/assistant_audio_0_waveform.png" id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:263/73;" width="263" height="73" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="--ltx-bg-color:#D2E6FA;" colspan="2">
<span id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:355.9pt;">
<span id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#D2E6FA;">Well, first we need to convert all the amounts to the same unit. Let’s use yuan. So, 50 cents is 0.5 yuan, 80 cents is 0.8 yuan, and 10 cents is 0.1 yuan. Now, we have 5 yuan, 4 yuan, 0.5 yuan, 0.8 yuan, 0.1 yuan, and 2.5 yuan. In ascending order, it’s 0.1 yuan, 0.5 yuan, 0.8 yuan, 2.5 yuan, 4 yuan, 5 yuan. That’s ten cents, 50 cents, 80 cents, 2 yuan and 50 cents, 4 yuan, 5 yuan. If you have any other questions about this or something else, feel free to let me know.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;height:0.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></td>
<td id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
<tr id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:366.2pt;">
<span id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.9.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.9.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A12.SS8.p1.pic1.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_top"></td></tr>
